A||||6||JohnnyK||How long does a rebuild take?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||02-02-2001||12:07 PM||||I've never done a rebuild before, but on my next car I am planning on hoppin up the engine before it goes in, so could anyone tell me how long I should expect? I don't know what I'd be doing to it, but I can assume the regulars (pistons, cam, maybe heads).. This would be for a v8..||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-02-2001||12:46 PM||||thats hard with no other info. Ive built an engine at the race track between races. Ive heard of guys taking months. you got machining to have done, may have to wait for parts, etc.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DrRodey||02-02-2001||01:17 PM||||The actual work doesn't tak all that long.  However it takes forever to get the exact parts you want, especially on a custom rebuild.  I'm learning that one first hand right now.  <P>------------------<BR>Hi... My names Dan, and i'm addicted to Fieros.<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTIBLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>AOL IM = drrodey<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">          <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||strick8||02-02-2001||01:33 PM||||Well I’m in the middle of a rebuild right now I would say if you want to do it fast have ALL the parts you need and have a machine shop picked out before you start. But you need to plan ahead for things such as you cant reuse the crank and other things not related to the rebuild such as a new clutch or motor mounts.||||reg||1
Z||000004||JohnnyK||02-02-2001||01:46 PM||||As you can see, I don't know much about rebuilding.. What do I need the machine shop for? I assume to redo the inside of the cylinder walls and stuff, but is that always necessary? Also, if you do that, won't you need bigger pistons? Or do all rebuild kits come with bigger pistons?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Hank is Here||02-02-2001||02:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>As you can see, I don't know much about rebuilding.. What do I need the machine shop for? I assume to redo the inside of the cylinder walls and stuff, but is that always necessary? Also, if you do that, won't you need bigger pistons? Or do all rebuild kits come with bigger pistons?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Jonny, <BR>The way I see it there is a difference between a rebuild and refresh.  A rebuild is having the cylinders bored, crank ground, block decked, alligned honed, ect, ect, ect.   I consider a refresh a hone of the cylinders, new rings and gaskets.  <BR>There would be no way to get away from a machine shop for a true rebuild.  I would say  that start to finish of a complete rebuild for me is about 4 weeks, I don't like to rush  at all and also want the correct parts.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||JohnnyK||02-02-2001||04:04 PM||||Well, I'd like to put in a different cam, forged pistons, maybe larger valves, (this is off the top of my head).. Maybe I should wait till I actually HAVE the engine so I can tell what needs to be done.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
